+<h2 class="h2">Who this serves</h2><div class="rule"></div><p>Brickell is Miami's financial district, and most Onyx bookings here follow that pattern: corporate accounts moving executives between office towers, meetings, and the airport, plus residents in the neighborhood's dense residential high-rises. It is one of the most walkable parts of Miami — many residents don't keep a car — which means the trips that do happen tend to be time-specific: a flight, a closing, a dinner reservation.</p><h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:40px">The geography</h2><div class="rule"></div><p>Brickell runs along Brickell Avenue between the Miami River to the north and roughly the Rickenbacker Causeway interchange to the south, with Biscayne Bay to the east and Interstate 95 to the west. North of the Miami River, US-1 continues into Downtown as Biscayne Boulevard, and the Financial District and the Metromover's Brickell Loop tie the two areas together.</p>
+</div>
+<div class="prose reveal">
+<h2 class="h2">Airport access</h2><div class="rule"></div><p>Miami International (MIA) is the closer, more frequently used airport from Brickell; the route depends on traffic and typically involves I-95 and/or SR 836 (the Dolphin Expressway) rather than a single fixed road. Fort Lauderdale-Hollywood (FLL) is a longer trip north but a reasonable option depending on your flight. President Donald J. Trump International Airport (DJT, formerly PBI) in West Palm Beach is generally reserved for a specific nonstop.</p><h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:40px">Trip types</h2><div class="rule"></div><p>Corporate accounts book recurring office-to-airport and office-to-meeting travel with consolidated billing. PortMiami cruise transfers are booked given the port's proximity across the bay. Event coverage for the Kaseya Center and Bayside Marketplace area, just north in Downtown, is booked the same way as any Brickell pickup.</p><h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:40px">A note on Brickell addresses</h2><div class="rule"></div><p>Brickell City Centre and Mary Brickell Village are both frequent pickup points but sit several blocks apart on Brickell Avenue and South Miami Avenue respectively — giving the specific property name at booking, rather than just "Brickell," avoids a pickup at the wrong entrance during a tight meeting window.</p>
